<!--
    Foreground layer of the adaptive launcher icon, drawn from the Flat Color weather family so
    the icon reads as part of the same design system:

      * Sun: disc r 16 at (46, 46) with the family's offset accent disc r 16 at (46, 47.5), plus
        eight round-capped rays from r 19.8 to r 23 at 22.5 deg + 45 deg * k - the same ray
        geometry as the 48 unit weather grid, scaled by 16 / 8.5.
      * Cloud: the one shared cloud silhouette of the weather family (three circles plus the flat
        base) at scale 1.5, translated by (24, 30); its shadow is the same path translated by
        (27, 33), exactly the offset trick of the weather drawables.

    Everything stays inside the 66 x 66 safe zone of the 108 unit adaptive icon canvas (x and y
    from 21 to 87), so circle, squircle and rounded rectangle masks all show sun and cloud.
    Colours are the light palette values of res/values/colors.xml, written out on purpose.
-->
